        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\cot x$; reciprocal",
          "worked": "$\\operatorname{cosec}x=\\frac{1}{\\sin x}$, $\\sec x=\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$ and $\\cot x=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}$. Cotangent is the reciprocal of tangent wherever both are defined, so the missing function is $y=\\cot x$ and the term is reciprocal.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-f2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p13-f2-b-text",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The graph ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "y=\\tan x",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " has asymptotes at ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "x=\\frac{k\\pi}{2}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", where ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "k",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is an o",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "dd",
                  "width": 14,
                  "joinPrevious": true
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " number.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "odd",
          "worked": "Since $\\tan x=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$, its vertical asymptotes occur where $\\cos x=0$: $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi=\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}$, for integer $n$. Thus $k$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
